question:
What is the output of the following code?

for i in range(3):
    print(i)

What does the following Python code do?

for i in range(6):
    if i % 2 == 0:
        continue
    print(i)

What will be the output of this nested loop?

for i in range(2):
    for j in range(3):
        print(i, j)

What is the output of the following code?

n = 0
while n < 3:
    for i in range(n):
        print(i, end='-')
    n += 1

What will be printed after execution of the Python code below?

matrix = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
for i in range(len(matrix)):
    for j in range(len(matrix[i])):
        if i == j:
            print(matrix[i][j])
